# Jarvis Project Context — client

# This file is read by the global Jarvis harness at the start of each
# inner-loop session. It provides project-specific rules to global agents
# (jarvis-executor, jarvis-reviewer) without modifying them.
#
# Sections:
#   ## Review Rules    → passed to jarvis-reviewer in every I2 brief
#   ## Executor Rules  → passed to jarvis-executor in every I1 brief
#
# Keep each section concise — every line here costs tokens per subagent call.
#
# TOKEN BUDGET (check with: node -e "console.log(Math.ceil(require('fs').readFileSync('jarvis.context.md','utf8').length/4))")
#   Whole file:        < 2,000 tokens  — this goes into EVERY I1 and I2 brief
#   ## Review Rules:   < 1,000 tokens  — reviewer brief overhead
#   ## Executor Rules: < 1,000 tokens  — executor brief overhead
# If you're referencing large skill files via @path, the token cost is the
# RESOLVED file content, not the @reference line itself — check the actual
# skill file sizes too. A 5,000-token code-reviewer.md referenced here means
# every single I2 review call carries that 5,000 tokens, every time.
#
# TIP — if you already have local skill files (e.g. .claude/skills/
# architecture.md, design-agent.md, code-reviewer.md), you don't have to
# duplicate their content here. Reference them instead:
#
#   ## Review Rules
#   @.claude/skills/architecture.md
#   @.claude/skills/code-reviewer.md
#
# inner-loop.md resolves @references to the full file content before
# building the reviewer/executor brief — one source of truth, no drift
# between this file and your skill files. The inline rules below are a
# fallback for projects that don't have separate skill files yet.

## Stack
Next.js 14 App Router · TypeScript strict · Redux Toolkit + RTK Query
CSS Variables · pnpm · Jest ESM

## Review Rules

**Data fetching**
- RTK Query for ALL remote data — no raw fetch(), no axios
- Every query MUST have providesTags
- Every mutation MUST have invalidatesTags

**Styling**
- CSS Variables only — var(--color-primary), var(--spacing-4)
- No hardcoded colors (#fff, rgb(), hsl())
- No inline styles (style={{ }})
- No Tailwind — this project uses CSS Variables

**Components**
- Server Components by default
- use client only when: useState, useEffect, event handlers, browser APIs
- No server-only imports inside use client files

**Security**
- Auth tokens: httpOnly cookies only, never localStorage or sessionStorage
- dangerouslySetInnerHTML: requires DOMPurify (exception — JSON-LD with own escaping)
- No console.log in production code

**TypeScript**
- strict: true — no implicit any
- Explicit return types on exported functions
- No @ts-ignore without comment explaining why

**Tests**
- jest.unstable_mockModule — never jest.mock
- Co-locate: src/components/Foo/__tests__/Foo.test.tsx
- ESM imports use .js extension

## Executor Rules

- Read max 2 files per step
- Use grep -n "symbol" src/ instead of reading whole files
- Never read: node_modules/, dist/, .next/, pnpm-lock.yaml
- Define RTK Query endpoints in src/store/api/ — one file per domain
- Co-locate tests: src/components/Foo/__tests__/Foo.test.tsx
